   "reasoning": "The patch charges T by index occurrences (Idx) instead of distinct POSITION vertices. Units change only where Idx != T. In work-base-meshopt (and all work-*-at-sum / sum-minus-1 copies) indices are [0,1,2] over 3 vertices, so Idx == T and the patch is inert there. In repeated-index-three-payloads, T rises from 3 to 3,999,990 per payload (vertex units about 200M each, about 600M total), which is still under the default containmentWorkUnits 2^32, so the base stays Contained. The units-minus-1 copy is already workLimit. The validate unit suite also passes: its work-caps test uses non-indexed POINTS (T == Idx == 1).",
